evals.prompt:
Our Rust note-taking app (wgpu + winit, our own UI) has a search box. Japanese users say they can't type in it, and someone noticed backspace on an emoji leaves garbage. Also add copy/paste and an 'Open file…' button. Here's the current key handler:

```rust
WindowEvent::KeyboardInput { event, .. } if event.state.is_pressed() => {
    match event.logical_key {
        Key::Named(NamedKey::Backspace) => { self.query.pop(); }
        _ => if let Some(t) = event.text { self.query.push_str(&t); }
    }
    if self.ctrl && event.logical_key == Key::Character("o".into()) {
        if let Some(path) = rfd::FileDialog::new().pick_file() { self.open(path); }
    }
}
```
